/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Wrapper base rule - NOT part of the prototype stylesheet.
   The prototype is a standalone document, so `html, body { height: 100% }`
   (re-scoped above to `.biblioteca-3d-root`) supplied the viewport-sized box
   that its absolutely positioned chrome (.top-bar, .chat-dock,
   .project-inspection-sheet, #webgl-viewport) positions against. Inside the
   Astro page nothing above the wrapper has a definite height, so the wrapper
   has to establish that box itself. `isolation: isolate` gives the component
   its own stacking context, keeping the prototype's internal z-index ladder
   below Base.astro's global navbar and the Chatbot FAB.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.biblioteca-3d-root {
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100vh;
  min-height: 420px;
}
